.TH UH7000CTL 1 "July 2026" "tascam-uh7000-linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
uh7000ctl \- manage and test the TASCAM UH-7000 Linux support package
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B uh7000ctl
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B uh7000ctl
configures and inspects the TASCAM UH-7000 USB audio interface on Linux.
The package selects USB configuration 2, registers the device with
.BR snd_usb_audio ,
and provides cautious diagnostics for the reverse-engineered vendor control
plane.
.PP
Commands that send USB vendor controls require root. Output tests are gated by
.B preflight
so they do not play audio while capture is clipped.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show USB configuration, bound kernel drivers, ALSA cards, and UH-7000 USB audio
stream descriptors.
.TP
.B configure
Switch the UH-7000 to USB Audio 2.0 configuration 2 and register the USB ID with
.BR snd_usb_audio .
.TP
.B control-status
Read the verified vendor selector status using request
.BR 0x49 .
This is a read-only control-plane check.
.TP
.BI "state-dump " [DIR]
Read the verified request
.B 0x55
vendor state pages
.B 0x1f00
and
.B 0x007c..0x007f
to
.IR DIR
or
.I /tmp
by default. The command writes raw 512-byte pages and JSON metadata. It is
read-only and does not scan unlisted page indices.
.TP
.BI "control-plan " NAME
Print decoded dry-run vendor transfer plans without sending USB controls.
Known names are
.BR quiet ,
.BR noise-mute ,
.BR adcdac ,
.BR routes ,
and
.BR f800 .
.TP
.B "control-plan f800"
Describe the decoded Windows
.B 0xf800
mixer/UI image path without generating or uploading a live image. The plan shows
the Windows upload/download IOCTLs, the six rate-specific
.B 0x42
blocks, the current
.B 0x4d
block, the footer checksum, and the corresponding request
.B 0x55
pages
.BR 0x007c..0x007f .
Actual image-byte regeneration remains in the offline research tool
.BR tools/uh7000_cpl_emulate.py .
.TP
.BI "f800-upload " IMAGE
Experimentally write a 2048-byte decoded
.B 0xf800
image to request
.B 0x55
pages
.BR 0x007c..0x007f .
The command requires root and refuses to run unless
.B UH7000_EXPERIMENTAL_0X55_WRITE=1
is present in the environment. It runs
.B preflight
before writing, saves the current pages to a backup file under
.IR /tmp ,
checks the image checksum, verifies every page by readback, and restores the
backup if capture clips immediately after upload.
.TP
.BI "f800-restore " IMAGE
Experimentally restore a saved 2048-byte
.B 0xf800
page image. This command also requires
.B UH7000_EXPERIMENTAL_0X55_WRITE=1
but does not require a clean preflight baseline because it is intended as a
rollback path after a bad
.B f800-upload
experiment.
.TP
.BI "preflight " [SEC]
Check the safe gate before output-routing tests. The command verifies USB
configuration, driver binding, ALSA stream shape, explicit playback feedback
mode, vendor control status, and capture clipping.
.TP
.BI "loopback-test " [SEC] " " [DBFS]
Run
.B preflight
first, then play a low 1 kHz tone through the 4-channel playback stream and
measure the return through the 6-channel capture stream. The command fails if
the return tone is not visible or if capture clips.
.TP
.BI "report " [SEC]
Print a JSON diagnostic report without playback or mixer writes. The report
includes USB state, ALSA stream text, parsed playback feedback mode, vendor
selector status, capture health, and a
.B safe_for_output_test
boolean.
.TP
.B quiet
Send the verified zeroed vendor mixer recovery blocks for requests
.B 0x4d
and
.BR 0x42 .
Use this only as a bounded recovery action after routing tests.
.TP
.BI "suppress-noise " [SEC]
Apply a Windows-derived, 64-byte, request
.B 0x4d
noise suppression block, then verify capture before and after. This command
does not play audio and does not send request
.BR 0x42 .
It cleared the local constant clipped output condition, but it is a recovery
gate rather than proof that USB playback routing is fixed.
.TP
.BI "recover " [SEC]
Run a no-playback recovery sequence for a clipped capture path: capture check,
.B quiet
mixer recovery, short wait, and a second capture check. The command exits
nonzero if capture still clips after the quiet recovery.
.TP
.BI "wait-clean " [TRIES] " " [SEC] " " [INTERVAL] " " [NTFY_TOPIC]
Poll
.B preflight
without playback or mixer writes until the UH-7000 reaches a clean capture
baseline. If
.I NTFY_TOPIC
is provided and
.BR curl (1)
is installed, send one ntfy.sh manual-action notification after the first failed
attempt.
.TP
.BI "input-noise " [SEC]
Capture from
.B hw:UH7000,0
without playback or mixer writes and report per-channel peak, RMS, DC offset,
clip polarity, zero-crossing rate, strongest spectral bins, and coarse band
power. This helps characterize analog output noise when outputs are patched back
to inputs.
.TP
.BI "capture-health " [SEC]
Record a short 48 kHz, 6-channel
.B S24_3LE
capture sample and print per-channel peak, RMS, full-scale clip counts, clipped
channel summary, and recovery recommendation.
.SH SAFETY
Do not run output-routing tests while the front-panel meter is solid red or
.B preflight
fails. Disconnect the physical output-to-input loopback and power-cycle the
UH-7000 before continuing if capture remains clipped.
.PP
Output-loopback tests also require the UH-7000 explicit feedback endpoint:
sync endpoint
.B 0x85
with
.B "Implicit Feedback Mode: No" .
If preflight reports implicit feedback, reload
.B snd_usb_audio
with
.B implicit_fb=N
for the test session before trusting output-routing results.
.PP
If the analog outputs emit steady noise before any manual control command runs,
disconnect the output-to-input loopback and verify a clean input baseline first.
That condition is not evidence that
.B uh7000ctl
sent a mixer write during hotplug; the automatic service only selects USB
configuration 2 and registers the device with
.BR snd_usb_audio .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/libexec/tascam-uh7000/tascam-uh7000-configure
Root helper used by udev/systemd hotplug handling.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/90-tascam-uh7000.rules
Udev rule that starts the configuration service for USB ID
.BR 0644:8048 .
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/tascam-uh7000-linux/
Installed README and reverse-engineering notes.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Commands return zero on success. Diagnostic and gated test commands return
nonzero when the UH-7000 is absent, the safe gate fails, capture clips, or a USB
control transfer fails.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aplay (1),
.BR arecord (1),
.BR curl (1),
.BR systemd-udevd (8)
